vtpl-dependency-floor ships data, not a library. There is nothing to
find_package() and nothing to link.

The floor is installed at:

    ${VCPKG_INSTALLED_DIR}/${VCPKG_TARGET_TRIPLET}/share/vtpl-dependency-floor/dependency-floor.json

Read it to verify that this manifest's builtin-baseline and overrides restate the
programme floor. vcpkg cannot do that for you: builtin-baseline and overrides are
honoured only in the top-level manifest, so a port cannot hand its pins down and
every consumer has to restate them. This file is what a consumer's check compares
its restatement against.

Check the RESOLVED versions too, not only the declared ones. A baseline bump can
move protobuf or abseil with no override naming either, and the declared block
will still look correct while the built binaries have moved.
